{
  "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8036-946a-ce7ff06748a9",
  "title": "Lombok for Boilerplate Reduction (@Data, @Getter, @Setter, @NoArgsConstructor, etc.)",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20924eb1ed548036946ace7ff06748a9",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-808b-bb69-dd5d431c14c3",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-84d8-d23d31782cfa",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "✅ 1. Core Concept (What & Why)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8041-ba83-f5f9baeca24c",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Lombok",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is a Java library that automatically generates common, repetitive code (called "
        ],
        [
          "boilerplate",
          [
            [
              "i"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ") like getters, setters, constructors, "
        ],
        [
          "toString()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "equals()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", and "
        ],
        [
          "hashCode()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-801e-b04c-d8ea838bcb5b",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It exists to reduce manual coding and keep Java classes clean and readable, especially in large Spring Boot applications where data models and DTOs (Data Transfer Objects) are common."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80e6-9219-ccb477c69618",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🔁 "
        ],
        [
          "Think of it like macros in C++",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " that save you from writing repetitive code for every class."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80cb-b270-d417c772eb09",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80af-bb03-d47212966157",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🎯 2. Key Interview Points"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-804e-a274-f7c54314d893",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What is Lombok and what problem does it solve?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d6-b887-c2ecaea38a6f",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "Reduces boilerplate code in Java classes like getters, setters, constructors, etc."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c4-80f6-e28a2fc621cc",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What do specific Lombok annotations like ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@Data",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@Getter",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@Setter",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", and ",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "@NoArgsConstructor",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ],
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " do?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8048-8b9d-e255875a543e",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "How does Lombok interact with Java compilers and IDEs?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80fc-9dfc-d319f568c4cc",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "It works via annotations and modifies bytecode at "
            ],
            [
              "compile time",
              [
                [
                  "i"
                ]
              ]
            ],
            [
              ", not runtime."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80c5-bfa7-c8db13f8b6f4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Is Lombok mandatory in Spring Boot? Why or why not?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "20924eb1-ed54-802f-b25f-e2bf4dad5e87",
          "type": "text",
          "richText": [
            [
              "No—it’s optional, but widely used in Spring Boot projects for convenience and readability."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8072-8738-d1d657a261f1",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80da-9b86-db2e0ef1d6ef",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🧑‍💻 3. Code Example"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8063-adb6-d95472ee7c40",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Let's compare a typical Java class with and without Lombok."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8093-8422-d674ff5aca02",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Without Lombok:"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-805c-9db5-e7f3dfba17e4",
      "type": "code",
      "richText": [
        [
          "public class User {\n    private String name;\n    private int age;\n\n    public User() {}\n\n    public User(String name, int age) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.age = age;\n    }\n\n    public String getName() { return name; }\n    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }\n\n    public int getAge() { return age; }\n    public void setAge(int age) { this.age = age; }\n\n    @Override\n    public String toString() {\n        return \"User{name='\" + name + \"', age=\" + age + \"}\";\n    }\n}\n"
        ]
      ],
      "language": "Java"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80cc-b7ca-ce0a8ff6dba2",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "With Lombok:"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-805d-a8bb-c6315f8a15b6",
      "type": "code",
      "richText": [
        [
          "import lombok.Data;\nimport lombok.NoArgsConstructor;\nimport lombok.AllArgsConstructor;\n\n@Data\n@NoArgsConstructor\n@AllArgsConstructor\npublic class User {\n    private String name;\n    private int age;\n}\n"
        ]
      ],
      "language": "Java"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80b8-9700-e616698e68f8",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "➡️ Lombok version does exactly the same but is shorter, cleaner, and easier to maintain."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-804d-9580-e124977011e3",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8065-a253-e71b62f09876",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "❓ 4. Common Interview Questions"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8029-ab69-f5137bbd69f1",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What is Lombok and how does it help in Spring Boot projects?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8097-a84c-ef0599a89765",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What does the "
        ],
        [
          "@Data",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " annotation do? What if I want only getters, not setters?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f2-88dc-cbc533ca1e35",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "How is "
        ],
        [
          "@AllArgsConstructor",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " different from "
        ],
        [
          "@NoArgsConstructor",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8025-9de9-df3c8ad13432",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Are there any downsides to using Lombok?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-b3e1-eb07b408aa43",
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Can Lombok cause issues in certain IDEs or build tools?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8094-93db-e74fd11778ed",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "👍 5. Best Practices & Pitfalls"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8050-ad9b-d3944aa2048c",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "✅ Best Practices"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80bf-a894-c3026f97608f",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use "
        ],
        [
          "@Data",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " only when you want a full-featured POJO (getters, setters, "
        ],
        [
          "toString()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", etc.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8060-8a14-e2665e1f99c5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Prefer specific annotations like "
        ],
        [
          "@Getter",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@Setter",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " if you need more control."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80b8-b348-f43b873772f9",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use constructor annotations like "
        ],
        [
          "@NoArgsConstructor",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "@AllArgsConstructor",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " when working with frameworks (e.g., Spring, JPA)."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8059-b5d7-d33459d5e837",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "❌ Common Pitfalls"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-802f-93da-f070ed532707",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Relying too heavily on "
        ],
        [
          "@Data",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " for entities can lead to unwanted side effects (e.g., infinite recursion in "
        ],
        [
          "toString()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " or "
        ],
        [
          "equals()",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ")."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8021-9b27-cd774a240180",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Forgetting to install Lombok plugin in your IDE (e.g., IntelliJ, Eclipse) may lead to red squiggly errors, even if the code compiles."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80b9-abdc-f6ed529a181a",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Using "
        ],
        [
          "@Setter",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " on immutable or sensitive fields (like passwords) can be a security risk."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80fb-9999-f065274ea3fd",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80cb-a44f-ebb08d439dd4",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🔗 6. Connection to Other Concepts"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
