      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot & Lombok",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ": Lombok is often used with DTOs, Entity classes, and Configuration classes to keep code short and maintainable."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8072-a973-f316260770f4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JPA/Hibernate",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ": "
        ],
        [
          "@NoArgsConstructor",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "@AllArgsConstructor",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " are especially useful for entity classes that need constructors for ORM (Object Relational Mapping)."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8029-a208-cf2bc5e9d030",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Validation & Jackson",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ": Lombok works well with libraries like Bean Validation ("
        ],
        [
          "@NotNull",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ") and Jackson ("
        ],
        [
          "@JsonProperty",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ") used in Spring Boot."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-805a-9325-d5a53c04353a",
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-809a-ad5d-df87e1400e03",
      "type": "sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "🗣 7. Quick Interview Answers"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80a5-b413-c14d11d7e94e",
      "type": "sub_sub_header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Q: What is Lombok and how is it useful in Spring Boot projects?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8056-8135-c276d6eabbc7",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A:",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8060-8fd0-e28062aa8d53",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Lombok is a Java library that reduces boilerplate code using annotations. In Spring Boot projects, it's commonly used in DTOs and entity classes to automatically generate getters, setters, constructors, and more. This makes the code cleaner, easier to read, and faster to write—especially when dealing with a lot of data models."
        ]
      ]
    },
